{
  "name": "Jeff Heaton Applications of Generative Artificial Intelligence",
  "category": "CS",
  "kind": "course",
  "desc": "Jeff Heaton's applications-focused generative AI course (2026, taught at Washington University) covering the OpenAI API and LangChain, prompting for code generation and debugging, LLM foundation models and text tasks, conversational memory, structured output parsers, RAG with ChromaDB and word embeddings, LangChain agents and tools, Kaggle and small LLMs, multimodal models and DALL-E image generation and editing, building StreamLit chat applications, OpenAI fine tuning, prompt engineering patterns from few shot and chain of thought to persona and verification patterns, and speech processing with text to speech and voice-enabled chatbots.",
